.nh
.TH "ORBIT" "1" "Aug 2026" "Orbit Developer Platform" "Orbit Platform Manual"

.SH NAME
orbit-port-check - Check repositories against the dev port registry (ports.yaml)


.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBorbit port check [flags]\fP


.SH DESCRIPTION
Scan compose files, package.json scripts, .env.example files, Go sources, Caddy files and TS/JS sources for ports 10000-17999 and report numbers the registry does not list (UNREGISTERED), retired numbers (RETIRED), binds in a repository the entry does not list (WRONG_REPO), binds of reserved slots (RESERVED) and compose publishes on all interfaces (OPEN_BIND, a warning unless --strict). Exit codes: 0 no findings, 1 at least one finding, 2 the registry is missing or a file could not be read.


.SH OPTIONS
\fB-h\fP, \fB--help\fP[=false]
	help for check

.PP
\fB--json\fP[=false]
	Print the result as a JSON envelope

.PP
\fB--root\fP=""
	workspace root holding handbook/agents/workspace/ports.yaml (default: the workspace containing the current directory)

.PP
\fB--strict\fP[=false]
	Treat OPEN_BIND warnings as failures


.SH OPTIONS INHERITED FROM PARENT COMMANDS
\fB--config\fP=""
	Custom path to Orbit CLI configuration file


.SH SEE ALSO
\fBorbit-port(1)\fP
